HST Office: an error in a VBA module no longer crashes the office when the Basic IDE shows it.

The IDE selects the module under its sub entry ("Microsoft Excel Objects", "Forms", ...) with
ImpFindEntry, which started from a fresh iterator that points at nothing. The VCL plugins (Windows,
gen, svp) dereference it, so a compile error or an uncaught runtime error in a real .xlsm or .docm
ended the office; gtk3 only logged a warning. The search now starts from the library entry.

License: this upstream file remains under its original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/ (regression file with a syntax error, run with the gen plugin).
